  "summary": "Messages queue cleared: 6 of 6 items closed.\n\n1. Evelyn Brooks, pt-0029 (red flag, handled first): she has black stools and feels lightheaded on standing while taking apixaban plus naproxen from urgent care. Created a stat Task to pool-rn-triage (task-t0001) and sent her an urgent message to go to the ED now. No medication changes made; the clinician needs to decide on apixaban/naproxen.\n\n2. Lena Park, pt-0028 (Reyes NP asked for amoxicillin-clavulanate for sinusitis): not prescribed. A 03/2024 St. Brigid urgent care note records hives, lip/throat swelling and a hoarse voice after Augmentin, treated with IM epinephrine. Her allergy list said NKDA. Per RBC-MED-04:\n   - Recorded an amoxicillin-clavulanate allergy (alg-t0016: unconfirmed, high criticality, reactions coded) and marked the NKDA entry inactive.\n   - Ordered no beta-lactam.\n   - Messaged Reyes with the finding and the RBC-CP-11 alternative, doxycycline 100 mg BID for 5–7 days. I did not place it; the prescriber decides, under a credentialed prescriber's name.\n   - Told the patient the prescription is on hold and the clinic will contact her today, and wrote a progress note (doc-t0020).\n\n3. Gloria Hayes, pt-0026 (lisinopril 20 mg): her last BMP (09/2025) is more than 12 months old, and she had a visit in 03/2026. Per RBC-RX-05 §1, sent a 30-day supply with 0 refills (mr-t0004, replaces the old order), ordered a BMP (sr-t0005) and told the patient.\n\n4. Frank Odum, pt-0027 (atorvastatin): not refilled because it conflicts with the chart. Cardiology stopped atorvastatin on 08/11/2026 for muscle aches and started rosuvastatin 10 mg. Per RBC-RX-05 §3, created a Task to you as PCP (task-t0007, focused on mr-t6-atorvastatin) to reconcile the med list; cardiology also wants a lipid panel around November. Told the patient.\n\n5. Samuel Price, pt-0030 (metformin 1000 mg BID): HbA1c 7.1% and eGFR 62 from 07/15/2026. Per RBC-RX-05 §2, renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0011) and told the patient.\n\n6. Marcus Webb, pt-0031: his request for a November morning BP check went to pool-scheduling as a Task (task-t0014), and he was told.",
